WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.048
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I’m twenty-six, so that means I’m Gen Z,

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:07.883
that is, the generation who were born between the nineteen nineties

00:00:07.996 --> 00:00:09.525
and the two thousand and tens.

00:00:10.007 --> 00:00:13.239
I haven’t read a book from the beginning to the end for years.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.776
I get three quarters of the way through, and then I look at the last page.

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:22.979
I don’t want to wait to find out how the story ends – I want to know now.

00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:24.872
It’s not just books.

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.325
I fast-forward to the middle of a song to hear the chorus –

00:00:28.546 --> 00:00:30.377
I don’t wait to hear the verses.

00:00:30.746 --> 00:00:34.374
Or I click to the middle of a film and watch a few minutes to see if

00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:38.127
I really want to spend two hours of my life watching it.

00:00:38.841 --> 00:00:40.807
I think it’s a Generation Z thing.

00:00:41.323 --> 00:00:43.223
My friends are just as bad as me.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.515
We send voice notes to each other because it’s quicker than texting,

00:00:47.872 --> 00:00:50.556
but we don’t actually listen to the whole recording.

00:00:51.197 --> 00:00:54.977
It’s easy to understand why – it’s because of social media.

00:00:55.629 --> 00:00:59.907
First it was photos that disappeared after three seconds on Snapchat,

00:01:00.343 --> 00:01:04.269
then it was Instagram stories with a fifteen-second time limit.

00:01:04.785 --> 00:01:08.042
Then, during the pandemic, it was TikTok –

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.803
the videos are only a few seconds long

00:01:11.024 --> 00:01:14.391
and the songs they feature are often played at double speed.

00:01:15.309 --> 00:01:19.010
My mum is always telling me to slow down, and yes,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:23.740
it’s true that my friends and I live life at a faster pace compared to our parents.

00:01:24.182 --> 00:01:26.734
But it’s nothing compared to the younger generation –

00:01:27.011 --> 00:01:29.449
their attention span is even shorter.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.740
Today’s teenagers really do live life at double speed.

00:01:34.155 --> 00:01:38.373
They just watch and listen to pretty much everything on fast-forward.